--- b3 medium.en: Every number in this video comes from the Social Security Administration, its earnings test page, its cost of living fact sheet, and its guide called How Work Affects Your Benefits. No news articles, no guesses. First, the basic idea, because it surprises almost everyone who hears it for the first time.
--- b3 large-v3: Every number in this video comes from the Social Security Administration, its earnings test page, its cost-of-living fact sheet, and its guide called How Work Affects Your Benefits. No news articles, no guesses. First, the basic idea, because it surprises almost everyone who hears it for the first time.
--- b4 medium.en: Here is the basic idea, and it is simpler than it sounds. If you claim your retirement benefit before your full retirement age and you keep working, Social Security compares your earnings with a yearly limit. Stay under the limit and nothing happens. Go over it and Social Security holds back part of your benefit. This rule is called the earnings test.
